                <pb facs="0355" n="247" xml:id="pg247"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1163/94: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Mayer</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-01-20T16:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 20,
                                1927—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received January 20—9:05
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>54. Supplementing my 42, January 17, 7 p.m. It is suggested that the Department
                    advise all American mission boards to instruct by telegraph their missionaries
                    in South and Central China promptly to withdraw from stations when directed to
                    do so by American diplomatic or consular officers, since experience has shown
                    the difficulty of inducing our nationals to heed the advice of Government
                    officials in this respect.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mayer</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
